EINVOICING_PDP_HELP2=Ovisno o odabranoj platformi, cijene mogu biti besplatne, fiksne ili po fakturi. Usporedite ih prije donošenja odluke.
EINVOICING_PDP_HELP3=Nakon što je odabrana pristupna točka, pojavljuje se njezina specifična konfiguracija.
EINVOICING_ROUTING_ID_HELP=Ovdje možete unijeti namjenski ID e-računa za ovu pristupnu točku. Obično vaš [SIREN] ili [SIREN_suffix] (gdje sufiks može biti SIRET, slobodan tekst...).<br>Ostavite prazno kako biste koristili zadani profesionalni ID vaše tvrtke (primjer SIREN u Francuskoj).
EINVOICING_BLOCK_INVOICE_NO_ROUTING_ID=Blokiraj generiranje/slanje računa za treće strane bez ručno postavljenog ID-a elektroničkog fakturiranja
EINVOICING_BLOCK_INVOICE_NO_ROUTING_ID_HELP=Obično koristimo ID e-računa koji se automatski generira iz podataka treće strane. Ovu opciju možete aktivirati kako biste onemogućili nagađanje ID-a e-računa i spriječili stvaranje ili slanje računa kada treća strana nema EKSPLICITNI ID elektroničkog računa. <br> Ako je onemogućeno (zadano, preporučeno), ID e-računa će se pogađati ako nije naveden (na primjer, korištenje SIRENT-a za francuske tvrtke).
EINVOICING_AUTO_SEND_ON_GENERATION=Automatically transmit to the AP on invoice validation
EINVOICING_AUTO_SEND_ON_GENERATION_HELP=Ako je omogućeno, e-račun se automatski prenosi na Pristupnu točku odmah nakon što je generiran (prilikom provjere valjanosti računa), bez korištenja gumba "Pošalji". Ne šalje se ponovno ako je račun već poslan (nema duplikata). Za omogućavanje generiranja u stvarnom vremenu potrebno je omogućiti generiranje.
EINVOICING_SKIP_B2C=Do not generate e-invoices for private individuals (B2C)
EINVOICING_SKIP_B2C_HELP=By default, only invoices generated to non elligible countries or generated from the Point of Sales modules does not generated Einvoices (they fall in the e-reporting scope). When enabled, e-invoicing is also skipped for some invoices generated from the backoffice if third parties are detected as private individuals (B2C). B2C transactions are out of the e-invoicing scope (they fall under e-reporting). Whether a third party is a company or a private individual is determined by Dolibarr itself (its own detection options), so there is nothing extra to configure here.
EINVOICING_VAT_EXIGIBILITY=VAT exigibility
EINVOICING_VAT_EXIGIBILITY_HELP=Tells when the VAT of an invoice falls due, hence the VAT point date code the document declares, the "VAT on debits" mention it carries and whether a cash-in is reported with the "Cashed in" (212) status. This module does not define that scheme, it reads the VAT mode of the Tax/VAT module setup. Current value, goods / services:
EINVOICING_VAT_POINT_DATE_CODE=VAT regime declared on the e-invoice (BT-8)
EINVOICING_VAT_POINT_DATE_CODE_HELP=VAT point date code carried by every VAT breakdown of the generated document. The French specification (XP Z12-012) makes it the field that declares the option for the payment of VAT on debits: code 5 is mandatory on the service invoices of a seller who took that option, and 72 tells the buyer the VAT falls due on collection. Leave on "Automatic" to derive it from the VAT mode above, which is what most sellers need: 5 on every document if the VAT mode says debits, 72 as soon as the document carries an operation taxed on collection, and nothing on a goods invoice of a seller with no option to declare. An explicit value is for a regime that mode cannot express: it applies to every generated document whatever it carries, and drives the "VAT on debits" legal mention and the scope of the "Cashed in" (212) status with it. A down payment invoice is the one exception and always declares 72, the VAT of a down payment falling due when it is collected whatever the regime. Code 29 says the same thing as 5 and is never derived automatically: the public portal only expects 5, and a 29 has to be reported to it as 5 (BR-FR-MAP-29).
EINVOICING_VAT_POINT_DATE_CODE_AUTO=Automatic (from the VAT mode of the Tax/VAT module)
EINVOICING_VAT_POINT_DATE_CODE_5=5 - Invoice date (VAT on debits)
EINVOICING_VAT_POINT_DATE_CODE_29=29 - Delivery date (VAT on debits)
EINVOICING_VAT_POINT_DATE_CODE_72=72 - Payment date (VAT on collection)
EINVOICING_MAX_FILE_SIZE_MB=Maximum e-invoice file size (MB)
EINVOICING_MAX_FILE_SIZE_MB_HELP=If set, a non-blocking warning is displayed when the generated e-invoice file (XML or PDF/A-3) exceeds this size. Leave empty or set to 0 to disable the check. Some Access Points limit the size of accepted files (e.g. 10 MB for Chorus Pro).
EINVOICING_TELL_CUSTOMER_PAYMENT_RECEIVED=Tell the customer when a payment has been received
EINVOICING_TELL_CUSTOMER_PAYMENT_RECEIVED_HELP=Send the "Payment received" status (212) to the Access Point when reception of a customer payment is confirmed (payment recorded in application).
EINVOICING_SEND_PAYMENT_SENT_STATUS=Tell the vendor when a supplier invoice is paid
EINVOICING_SEND_PAYMENT_SENT_STATUS_HELP=When enabled, the "Payment transmitted" (211) status is sent to the Access Point as soon as a supplier invoice received through the platform is classified as paid in Dolibarr, with the amount paid and its date. It is sent once per invoice. This status is optional in the reform (it is a courtesy to your vendor) and each one costs a flow on your Access Point, hence disabled by default.
EINVOICING_SEND_APPROVED_ON_VALIDATION=Tell the vendor when a supplier invoice is validated
EINVOICING_SEND_APPROVED_ON_VALIDATION_HELP=No by default, so the "Approved" (205) status is sent to the Access Point only if setup. If on, it is sent once per invoice, and never on an invoice already answered with "Approved" or "Refused". A failure to send never undoes the validation.
EInvoiceFileSizeExceedsLimit=The generated e-invoice file (%s MB) exceeds the configured size limit (%s MB). Your Access Point may reject this file.
EINVOICING_USE_BILLING_CONTACT_AS_BUYER=Use the billing contact as the e-invoice buyer
EINVOICING_USE_BILLING_CONTACT_AS_BUYER_HELP=For French invoices only. When enabled, if the invoice has a billing contact (contact of type "Customer invoice contact / BILLING"), this contact is used as the buyer in the generated XML instead of the invoice thirdparty. <br> If the contact belongs to a different thirdparty (e.g. the head office is a separate legal entity), the whole buyer party - name, address, SIREN/SIRET, VAT number and routing ID - is rebuilt from that thirdparty. <br> If the contact belongs to the same thirdparty, only the buyer name/address are overridden while the SIREN, VAT number and routing remain those of the invoice thirdparty. <br> Disabled by default. Note: the XML buyer will then differ from the invoice thirdparty shown in Dolibarr. <br> This option is only about the buyer party: the billing contact itself is always written as the buyer contact (BG-9) of the generated XML, whether the option is enabled or not.
